{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.6e372d8de5","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-0","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Beatriz Adeyemi is a marine biologist.</li><li>Adeyemi wanted to find out whether noise from passing ships affects how often humpback whales sing.</li><li>Adeyemi recorded whale songs in a busy shipping lane and in a quiet bay for two months.</li><li>Adeyemi found that whales in the shipping lane sang about 40 percent less often.</li><li>Adeyemi concluded that ship noise may interfere with whale communication.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Adeyemi recorded whale songs in a busy shipping lane and in a quiet bay for two months.","Adeyemi found that whales in the shipping lane sang about 40 percent less often.","Marine biologist Beatriz Adeyemi set out to learn whether noise from passing ships affects how often humpback whales sing.","Adeyemi concluded that ship noise may interfere with whale communication."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.0b9174f4b2","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-5","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Omar Duarte is a marine biologist.</li><li>Duarte wanted to find out whether noise from passing ships affects how often humpback whales sing.</li><li>Duarte recorded whale songs in a busy shipping lane and in a quiet bay for two months.</li><li>Duarte found that whales in the shipping lane sang about 40 percent less often.</li><li>Duarte concluded that ship noise may interfere with whale communication.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Marine biologist Omar Duarte set out to learn whether noise from passing ships affects how often humpback whales sing.","Duarte found that whales in the shipping lane sang about 40 percent less often.","Duarte concluded that ship noise may interfere with whale communication.","To investigate the question, Duarte recorded whale songs in a busy shipping lane and in a quiet bay for two months."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.623b7bb03b","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-12","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Amara Asante is a psychologist.</li><li>Asante wanted to find out whether taking short breaks improves students' focus during long study sessions.</li><li>Asante had one group of students take a five-minute break every half hour while another group studied without breaks.</li><li>Asante found that students who took breaks answered more practice questions correctly.</li><li>Asante concluded that brief breaks may help people stay focused.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Asante had one group of students take a five-minute break every half hour while another group studied without breaks.","Asante concluded that brief breaks may help people stay focused.","Psychologist Amara Asante set out to learn whether taking short breaks improves students' focus during long study sessions.","Asante found that students who took breaks answered more practice questions correctly."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.7edecf330e","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-18","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Diego Haddad is an agricultural scientist.</li><li>Haddad wanted to find out whether planting clover between rows of corn reduces the need for fertilizer.</li><li>Haddad grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons.</li><li>Haddad found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer.</li><li>Haddad concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Agricultural scientist Diego Haddad set out to learn whether planting clover between rows of corn reduces the need for fertilizer.","To investigate the question, Haddad grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons.","Haddad concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.","Haddad found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.a0b7451d0d","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-22","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Priya Takeda is an agricultural scientist.</li><li>Takeda wanted to find out whether planting clover between rows of corn reduces the need for fertilizer.</li><li>Takeda grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons.</li><li>Takeda found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer.</li><li>Takeda concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Takeda found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer.","Agricultural scientist Priya Takeda set out to learn whether planting clover between rows of corn reduces the need for fertilizer.","To investigate the question, Takeda grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons.","Takeda concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.e2aee1a168","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-34","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Tomás Takeda is an entomologist.</li><li>Takeda wanted to find out whether bees prefer flowers of a particular color.</li><li>Takeda set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow.</li><li>Takeda found that bees visited the blue feeders most often.</li><li>Takeda concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Takeda set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow.","Takeda found that bees visited the blue feeders most often.","Entomologist Tomás Takeda set out to learn whether bees prefer flowers of a particular color.","Takeda concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.631b6522f7","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-61","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Viktor Varga is an astronomer.</li><li>Varga wanted to find out whether a distant star's brightness changes on a regular schedule.</li><li>Varga measured the star's brightness every night for eighteen months.</li><li>Varga found that the star dimmed slightly about every 42 days.</li><li>Varga concluded that an orbiting planet may be passing in front of the star.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Astronomer Viktor Varga set out to learn whether a distant star's brightness changes on a regular schedule.","Varga concluded that an orbiting planet may be passing in front of the star.","To investigate the question, Varga measured the star's brightness every night for eighteen months.","Varga found that the star dimmed slightly about every 42 days."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.ad715e012c","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-92","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ingrid Castellano is a hydrologist.</li><li>Castellano wanted to find out whether wetlands reduce flooding downstream.</li><li>Castellano compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms.</li><li>Castellano found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.</li><li>Castellano concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Castellano concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods.","Hydrologist Ingrid Castellano set out to learn whether wetlands reduce flooding downstream.","Castellano found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.","To investigate the question, Castellano compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.e05f60fb06","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-110","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Priya Mensah is a primatologist.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether young chimpanzees learn to use tools by watching adults.</li><li>Mensah observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.</li><li>Mensah found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.</li><li>Mensah concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Mensah found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.","To investigate the question, Mensah observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.","Primatologist Priya Mensah set out to learn whether young chimpanzees learn to use tools by watching adults.","Mensah concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.2ffbb318cb","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-123","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Leila Ferreira is an ornithologist.</li><li>Ferreira wanted to find out whether birds that migrate farther have longer wings.</li><li>Ferreira measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.</li><li>Ferreira found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.</li><li>Ferreira concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Ferreira concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.","Ferreira found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.","To investigate the question, Ferreira measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.","Ornithologist Leila Ferreira set out to learn whether birds that migrate farther have longer wings."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.9e5cce96c8","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-153","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Idris Nakamura is a climate scientist.</li><li>Nakamura wanted to find out whether light-colored roofs reduce indoor temperatures.</li><li>Nakamura compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs.</li><li>Nakamura found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.</li><li>Nakamura concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Nakamura concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.","Climate scientist Idris Nakamura set out to learn whether light-colored roofs reduce indoor temperatures.","Nakamura found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.","To investigate the question, Nakamura compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."}
